// `Title:Text { colour: 0xFFFFFF }` -- a styled variant.
//
// A variant gives a component a name and a set of non-geometry defaults. What it
// may *not* carry is geometry: dimensions and anchors stay in the layout, which
// is the rule that keeps a screen's shape readable in one place (IDML_GAME.md
// section 6). Nothing enforces that yet -- the parser records whatever props are
// written and the UI resolver is where the restriction belongs.
//
// It is told apart from a declaration by the colon, and it has to be, because
// `Title` is not a keyword and never will be: an author names these. Before this
// existed, each variant produced one "unknown declaration" per token in it --
// four diagnostics for two lines of perfectly good idml.

par_dvar(int[] pos, string name, int ln) {
  int nd = 0;
  if (par_is(pos, ":") = 1) {
    nd = par_variant(pos, name);
  } else {
    nd = par_dbad(pos, name);
  }
} return int nd;

par_variant(int[] pos, string name) {
  par_next(pos);
} return int par_variant2(pos, name, par_text(pos));

// `bn` and not `base`: `base` is already an int elsewhere in the program, and a
// name carries one type across the whole of it.
//
// The base's name is kept as the first child rather than in a slot of its own:
// ast_new_kids takes one text and a list, and a variant of a variant would want
// the same shape anyway.
par_variant2(int[] pos, string name, string bn) {
  int[] ks = [ast_new_k(ast_k_ident(), bn)];
  par_next(pos);
} return int par_vbody(pos, name, ks);
